div min-h-screen overflow-x-hidden antialiased bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-300 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed selection:bg-purple-500/30
	div max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-10
		header flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 py-6 sm:py-8
			a href="#top" flex items-center gap-2.5 no-underline shrink-0 text-zinc-100 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity
				img src="./favicon.svg" alt="" width="28" height="28" w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded
				span text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight
					"equilibrium"
			nav flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-1 text-xs
				a href="https://crates.io/crates/equilibrium-ffi" text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-100 no-underline transition-colors target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
					"crates.io"
				a href="https://github.com/tschk/equilibrium" text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-100 no-underline transition-colors target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
					"GitHub"
		main pt-8 pb-14 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-20
			section mb-16
				p text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-purple-400 mb-4
					"equilibrium-ffi 0.3 · ISC · Rust + C ABI"
				h1 text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-zinc-100 tracking-tight leading-tight max-w-2xl mb-5
					"Load foreign code with "
					span text-purple-400
						"one call"
				p text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-7
					"Point equilibrium at a source file — V, Zig, C, C++, C#, Rust, D, Nim, Odin, Hare, or TypeScript — and it detects the language, compiles it to C, and loads the result. Rust bindings come out the same door."
				div flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-10
					a href="https://github.com/tschk/equilibrium" inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-purple-500 hover:bg-purple-400 text-zinc-950 text-xs font-semibold px-4 py-2.5 no-underline transition-colors target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						"Get started"
						span aria-hidden="true"
							"→"
					a href="https://crates.io/crates/equilibrium-ffi" inline-flex items-center rounded-md border border-zinc-700 hover:border-zinc-500 text-zinc-200 text-xs px-4 py-2.5 no-underline transition-colors target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						"equilibrium-ffi on crates.io"
				div grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 mb-10
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 overflow-hidden
						div px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500
							"rust"
						pre p-4 m-0 text-[11px] sm:text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 whitespace-pre overflow-x-auto
							"use equilibrium_ffi::load;\n\nlet lib = load(\"examples/c-ffi/mathlib.c\")?;\nlib.output_path.display() // ready to link"
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 overflow-hidden
						div px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500
							"terminal"
						pre p-4 m-0 text-[11px] sm:text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 whitespace-pre overflow-x-auto
							"$ eq check\n$ eq install zig nim odin\n$ eq build --release\n$ eq generate abi.h --consumer scriptc"
			section id="pipeline" mb-16
				h2 block text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500 mb-4
					"Pipeline"
				div grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-5
						p block text-purple-400 text-xs font-semibold mb-2
							"01 · Detect"
						p block text-zinc-400 text-xs leading-relaxed
							"Eleven languages mapped by extension. find_compiler() locates each toolchain on PATH — or eq install puts it there."
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-5
						p block text-purple-400 text-xs font-semibold mb-2
							"02 · Compile to C"
						p block text-zinc-400 text-xs leading-relaxed
							"Every source compiles to a C intermediate with the right flags — -fPIC and ReleaseFast for Zig objects, library archives for scriptc."
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-5
						p block text-purple-400 text-xs font-semibold mb-2
							"03 · Bind"
						p block text-zinc-400 text-xs leading-relaxed
							"The C surface becomes Rust extern \"C\" declarations — or consumer wrappers in the very languages you started from."
			section id="languages" mb-16
				h2 block text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500 mb-4
					"Languages"
				p block text-zinc-400 max-w-2xl mb-5
					"Producers compile to the C ABI. Consumers take any C header and generate in-process FFI declarations. scriptc does both directions."
				div flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-6
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"V"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"Zig"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"C"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"C++"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"C#"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"Rust"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"D"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"Nim"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"Odin"
					span rounded border border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-900/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-zinc-300
						"Hare"
					span rounded border border-purple-500/50 bg-purple-500/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-purple-300
						"TypeScript · scriptc"
				div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 overflow-hidden
					div px-4 py-2 border-b border-zinc-800 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500
						"one header → every consumer"
					pre p-4 m-0 text-[11px] sm:text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 whitespace-pre overflow-x-auto
						"$ eq generate crepuscularity_abi.h --consumer rust     # extern \"C\" block\n$ eq generate crepuscularity_abi.h --consumer zig      # @cImport aliases\n$ eq generate crepuscularity_abi.h --consumer scriptc  # bindings.ts + --ffi manifest"
			section id="ecosystem"
				h2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-zinc-500 mb-4
					"Ecosystem"
				div grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-5 flex flex-col
						div flex items-center justify-between mb-3
							p text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold
								"rig"
							p text-zinc-500 text-[11px]
								"tschk/rig"
						p block text-zinc-400 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4
							"Cross-language native dependency manager. Detects the host language, adds crates from the CLI, and exposes them in-process through equilibrium-ffi — including TypeScript hosts via scriptc."
						div mt-auto
							p block text-[11px] text-zinc-500 mb-2
								"cargo install rigpkg"
							a block w-fit href="https://github.com/tschk/rig" text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 text-xs no-underline target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
								"github.com/tschk/rig →"
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-5 flex flex-col
						div flex items-center justify-between mb-3
							p text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold
								"eqts"
							p text-zinc-500 text-[11px]
								"tschk/eqts"
						p block text-zinc-400 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4
							"One Rust API for TypeScript. Annotate with #[eqts::export] and run the same library in Node, Bun, Deno, and WebAssembly — records, results, async, streams, and object proxies included."
						div mt-auto
							p block text-[11px] text-zinc-500 mb-2
								"cargo install cargo-eqts"
							a block w-fit href="https://github.com/tschk/eqts" text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 text-xs no-underline target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
								"github.com/tschk/eqts →"
					div rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/60 p-5 flex flex-col
						div flex items-center justify-between mb-3
							p text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold
								"eqswift"
							p text-zinc-500 text-[11px]
								"tschk/eqswift"
						p block text-zinc-400 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4
							"Two lines to FFI Rust into Swift. UniFFI proc-macros plus cargo eqswift emit Swift bindings from annotated Rust — no UDL files, no build.rs."
						div mt-auto
							p block text-[11px] text-zinc-500 mb-2
								"eqswift = \"0.1\" + uniffi"
							a block w-fit href="https://github.com/tschk/eqswift" text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 text-xs no-underline target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
								"github.com/tschk/eqswift →"
		footer border-t border-zinc-800 mt-4
			div max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-10 py-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 text-[11px] text-zinc-500
				p
					"equilibrium · ISC · built with crepuscularity + moonshine"
				div flex items-center gap-4
					a href="https://github.com/tschk/equilibrium" text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-100 no-underline target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						"GitHub"
					a href="https://docs.rs/equilibrium-ffi" text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-100 no-underline target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						"docs.rs"
					a href="https://tsc.hk" text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-100 no-underline target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
						"tsc.hk"
